<LegalPage title="Site Terms" kicker="For everyone who visits">
<p class="lede">If you’re here to find art and go see it, this is the page that covers you. It’s short, because the deal is simple.</p>

<h3>Using the site</h3>
<p>It’s free, and you don’t need an account to look around. Use the forms for what they’re for. Spam, harassment, or trying to break the site gets you blocked.</p>

<h3>The art belongs to the artists</h3>
<p>Share links to anything you like. That’s the point. But the artwork belongs to the people who made it, so don’t copy it, download it, or reuse it without the artist’s permission. The lessons, writing, and design of the site belong to Artists Are Jerks, so ask before reusing those too. If you find your own work posted here by someone else, see <a href="/copyright/">Copyright</a>.</p>

<h3>Showings can change</h3>
<p>Artists tell us where their work is hanging, and they check in to keep it current. But shows close early, cafés change their hours, and pieces sell off the wall. If you’re making a special trip, check with the venue first.</p>

<h3>Buying art</h3>
<p>If you want a piece, you work that out with the artist. We’re not part of the sale. We don’t hold money, and we can’t guarantee a piece, a price, or a delivery.</p>

<h3>Venues</h3>
<p>The places listed here are independent. We don’t run them, and listing one doesn’t mean we vouch for everything about it. Accessibility details come from the venue or the artist and may be incomplete.</p>

<h3>Writing to artists and following them</h3>
<p>When you send a message, the artist gets your name and email so they can write back. When you follow an artist, you’ll get an email when they have new work up, and every one of those emails has a way to stop. The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Notice</a> has the details.</p>

<h3>Other websites</h3>
<p>Artists and venues link to their own sites. Those sites aren’t ours, and their rules apply there.</p>

<h3>The legal part</h3>
<p>The site comes as it is, without promises that it’ll always be available or error-free. As far as the law allows, we aren’t responsible for losses that come from using it, including a trip to a show that turned out to be over. Oregon law applies.</p>

<h3>If you have an account</h3>
<p>Artists also agree to the <a href="/artist-terms/">Artist Terms</a>. Everyone follows the <a href="/guidelines/">Community Guidelines</a>.</p>

<h3>Changes and questions</h3>
<p>The date at the top shows the current version. Questions or problems: info@artistsarejerks.com.</p>
</LegalPage>
